``peat pillage`` can now mount and search disk images on Windows. VHD, VHDX, and ISO images are mounted read-only with ``Mount-DiskImage``, and other formats (raw, VMDK, qcow2) are converted to VHDX with ``qemu-img`` first. System folders such as ``Windows`` are only skipped in the root of a drive, mounted filesystem, or image, and are matched case-insensitively. Searches don't follow Windows junctions, and no longer fail on unreadable subfolders or locked files. Volumes encrypted with BitLocker are detected and reported, instead of failing with a generic error.
